  "wikitext": "{{Short description|Species of fern}}\n{{Speciesbox\n| image = Davallia_bullata_1_ies.jpg\n| image_caption = Davallia bullata\n| genus = Davallia\n| species = bullata\n| authority = Wall. ex Hook.\n}}\n\n'''''Davallia bullata''''', the '''squirrel's-foot fern''',<ref name=BSBI07>{{BSBI 2007 |accessdate=2014-10-17 }}</ref> is a fern in the family [[Davalliaceae]] found mainly in Japan and China. It grows well in shady places. It grows from 20 to 35&nbsp;cm. It has deciduous bullata and its leaflets are linear.\n\n==References==\n{{reflist}}\n* ''The Botanical Magazine'', Vol. XXIII. January, 1909.\n* ''Flora of Japan'', 1957, p.&nbsp;22.\n\n{{Taxonbar|from=Q5799718}}\n\n[[Category:Davalliaceae]]\n[[Category:Flora of China]]\n[[Category:Flora of Japan]]\n\n\n{{Polypodiales-stub}}",
